==English==
===Etymology===
From [[w:Irish language|Irish]][[Category:Irish derivations]] naigín, or [[w:Gaelic language|Gaelic]][[Category:Gaelic derivations]] noigean. Compare with [[nog]].

===Pronunciation===
*Rhymes: [[Rhymes:English:-ɒɡɪn|-ɒɡɪn]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

#A [[small]] [[mug]], [[cup]] or [[ladle]]. 
#{{dated}} A measure equivalent to a gill. Also possibly linked to the phrase "naggan of vodka"(a small bottle of vodka).
#{{slang}} the [[head]]

